# SpaceRank NYC runs with zero required environment variables today —
# every data source used at request time is a free, keyless public API
# (NYC GeoSearch, NYC Open Data PLUTO/subway snapshots).
#
# This file documents variables that PLANNED features would read, so the
# pattern (env var in, never hardcoded) is established before they're needed.
# None of these are required to run the app locally or to deploy it.

# Durable lead storage (see app.py's /api/leads — currently logs structured
# JSON to stdout since Vercel functions have no writable disk). Would switch
# to Vercel Postgres or Vercel KV; the connection string goes here, never
# in code.
# DATABASE_URL=

# The frontend's optional Google Maps mode (index.html's GMAPS_KEY constant)
# is a browser-side, HTTP-referrer-restricted key, not a backend secret — it
# stays a hardcoded constant in index.html by design (see the comment above
# it), not an env var, because it's meant to be publicly visible in the
# shipped JS. Restrict it to your domain in Google Cloud Console before
# adding one.
